  "body": "Found in the fact check of PR #3652. The refusal is there: `EditOperationParams::new` runs `named_refusal` (`crates/app/src/commands/operation/edit.rs:114`), which calls `trochoidal_pass_start_refusal` (`crates/app/src/operation/types/sane.rs:87`), and MCP `edit_operation` builds the command with `new` (`crates/app/src/mcp/edit.rs:324`). But the test `adaptive_pass_start::trochoidal_adaptive_refuses_a_forced_pass_start_by_name` asserts the refusal at generate and through a direct call of `named_refusal`; no test goes through the MCP edit door. **Wanted:** one MCP test with `Client::refused`: `edit_operation` with `pass_start: \"inside\"` on a Trochoidal 2D Adaptive is refused by name, and the reverse order (an operation with `inside`, then the method is set to Trochoidal) is refused too. The operation does not change.",
